Z||000007||DR650SE||11-20-2001||12:32 AM||||First replace the relay its only a few $'s The limit switch may be out, I dont know where it is but i think in the motor?  I dont even know it there is one, When I swapped a motor for the same problem it worked.  The ground stuff is the plastic gear. My geuss is alimit switch goes out and it keeps spinning damaging the plastic gear.  Try to figure the problem out before the rebuild or you may damage the new gear.  My $.02.  Keep me updated.<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||4
Z||000008||SKIDMARK||11-20-2001||01:02 AM||||Sounds like limit switch. The relay on the inside of the left fender is the main. If your lights go up and down, then you don't need that one. If the limit switch goes bad, you'll rip the teeth off that nylon gear in the actuator, or if the teeth wear out, the limit switch won't work and the motor keeps running, usually in the down direction. In any case, if the lights go up and down then the relays are good. The problem has to be the limit switch unless someone crossed some wires or something.||||reg||1
Z||000009||tgowens||11-20-2001||01:03 AM||||The motors are designed to stop when the headlight travel is limited - If you look at the arm from the headlight bucket to the motor you will see a "cam" on the motor shaft connected to that arm. The tip on that cam contacts a rubber stop in either the up or down position creating the resistance needed to stop the motor.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||NEO Cesek Racing||11-20-2001||03:25 PM||||ok those last two posts have me all confused. i had some green ground up gunk inside the motor when i opened it up. i'm assuming i need that rebuild kit that comes with a new gear and new green bumpers.  if this is true i will order one. i'm not clear on all this relay stuff.  i was about to order the kit but if there's something i should be checking before i do, i'd like to know. the headlight goes up and down fine, but the manual control knob just spins when it's in the down position. that's my only problem. but from what i can tell, i just need the kit. any input would be great. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000011||NEO Cesek Racing||11-22-2001||03:15 AM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000012||StuGood||11-22-2001||05:15 PM||||(Sigh) It's not any of the relays' jobs to <B>stop</B> the headlight motor.  A limit switch inside the motor does that job.  The limit switch is supposed to shut off the motor when the headlight motor encounters (mechanical) resistance.<P>Since your headlight motor won't quit spinning, it's either not encountering enough mechanical resistance at the end of its travel (e.g.- gear is worn or stripped), or the limit switch isn't working right.  <P>So order Rodney's kit and quit worrying about relays.  Since you found pulverized green crud inside the motor, it needs rebuilt.  You won't be wasting your money.  If you want to learn more about how the headlight system works, visit the Michigan Fiero Club website.||||reg||1
